<Project>

  <!--
    Deliberately empty. Directory.Build.props discovery stops at the first file found walking up,
    so this shields the imported Xamarin sources from the repository-wide settings in the root
    Directory.Build.props. legacy/ must keep building exactly as it did in Xamarinme; enabling
    Nullable across it, for instance, would bury the four advisory warnings that matter under
    dozens that do not.

    There is deliberately no matching Directory.Build.targets. The root one only writes a
    Mauime.ReferencePaths.txt beside each assembly, which changes nothing about how the code
    compiles and is what lets the API baseline resolve the legacy assemblies' 2.2.0-era
    dependencies. This file is the only one added under legacy/; nothing imported has been edited.
  -->

</Project>
